# Hazard Course walk route (route source; syntax and semantics:
# docs/formats/route-bytecode.md). Converted from the old tree's generated
# walk n64/port/test/out/hl-walk-t0a0_.cfg (gen_hl_walk_route.py, audit:
# CLEAN): t0a0 -> t0a0a -> t0a0b1 -> t0a0b2 -> t0a0c -> t0a0b -> t0a0c ->
# t0a0d. Each visit: god on, stats, a setpos into every trigger_once /
# trigger_multiple brush (masters and scripts decide what fires), stats,
# then setpos hops through the seam's trigger into its switch box and
# waitmap for the next map. Conversion: the old `god` (no argument) is
# `god 1` (the generator's rule: set, never toggle); the old `hl_trace 1`
# (an old-engine console switch logging entity fires) has no route op and
# is dropped. Positions are map-local. The old walk booted with `map t0a0`
# on the runner's command line (run_hl_walk_host.sh); here that is the
# route's `startmap t0a0` (without it New Game boots the campaign start).
startmap t0a0
